 ## Background
-The method was introduced by Jussi Rääsen, Mario Botsch, Carsten Dachsbacher, and Mark Pauly [S2, unofficial]. It addresses limitations in previous point rendering techniques by Heckbert and Zwicker, which used affine approximations of the perspective projection that were exact only at the kernel center [S2, unofficial]. The source is an unofficial record from EPFL [S2, unofficial]. The SPH perspective fix described in [S1] is a related implementation detail in the pynbody library, correcting integration along the oblique ray.
+The method was introduced by Jussi Rääsen, Mario Botsch, Carsten Dachsbacher, and Mark Pauly [S2, unofficial]. It addresses limitations in previous point rendering techniques by Heckbert and Zwicker, which used affine approximations of the perspective projection that were exact only at the kernel center [S2, unofficial]. The source is an unofficial record hosted at EPFL, though the authors are affiliated with MIT, Helsinki University, TU Aachen, and FAU Erlangen-Nürnberg [S2, unofficial]. The SPH perspective fix described in [S1] is a related implementation detail in the pynbody library, correcting integration along the oblique ray.
 
